    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0221" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg139"/>

                <head>Mr. Marsh to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 109.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Turin,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 22, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I mentioned in a recent despatch that I had
                    applied to the Italian government to permit the temporary establishment of a
                    depot for naval stores of the United States at Cagliari.</p>
                <p>I have received a reply, a translation of which is enclosed herewith. The
                    decision of the Navy Department to defer for the present the employment of
                    storehouses on shore, renders it unnecessary to prosecute the subject further,
                    and I have notified the Italian government accordingly.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE P. MARSH.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d136-a1.xml" xpointer="d136-a1"/>
